The important algorithmic upgrade is:

A(e|H_t)=
\mathbb E[\text{fitness}|e,H_t]
+\beta_t U(e)
+\gamma N(e)
-\lambda_C C(e)
-\lambda_R R(e)

where history H_t contains prior trials plus metadata. Randomness proposes futures; the learned model predicts which futures are promising; uncertainty deliberately preserves exploration.

That turns randomness from:

\text{randomness}\rightarrow\text{variation}

into:

\boxed{
\text{randomness}
+\text{memory}
+\text{metadata}
+\text{prediction}
\rightarrow
\text{guided possibility generation}
}

The README also leaves a clean hook for AI metadata such as operator sequence, representation, Seal IDs, route, invariants preserved, semantic distance, failure mode, surprise, cost, risk, and Reality score.

That is where it begins becoming the executable Metamap learner rather than just an optimizer.